       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the accepted maximum, so I need you to confirm or revise it first.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** Doses at this level carry a serious risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function. A 70 kg patient is not an exception.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day). This is a common conservative standard.\n2. **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day). This is the labeled maximum.\n3. **Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day).\n\nIf 2000 mg three times daily is what you intended, for example because of a typo or a protocol I don't know about, tell me. I'll enter whichever dose you confirm, and I'll add a note documenting the rationale if you want one."
      }
